# MOSCA's own self-scan.
#
# `examples/vulnerable-app/` is intentionally insecure: it exists so the
# scanner can be demonstrated without pointing it at real code.
#
# `test/` contains rule fixtures — MD5, SHA-1 and RC4 strings appear there on
# purpose to prove the rules fire. Neither directory is part of the shipped
# product, so the CI self-scan excludes them.
examples/
test/
